+`session_abort` notifies handlers synchronously on explicit `AgentSession.abort()`, even while idle, before Pi cancels native operations. Idle manual compaction does not notify; compaction still cancels an active run. Use it to disarm extension-owned recovery or deferred delivery. Returned promises are not awaited; thrown errors and rejected promises are reported without preventing cancellation. Reentrant `ctx.abort()` does not emit it twice. Unclaimed idle Escape, SDK abort, and RPC abort use this route.
+
 `before_agent_start` exposes both the current prompt and its structured `systemPromptOptions`. Prefer changing prompt sections, selected tools, or guidelines so Pi can append a transcript delta. Returning `systemPrompt`, or setting `forceSystemPrompt`, replaces the whole prompt for that run while the transcript continues recording the structured sections. Providers receive the forced text as their leading system prompt.
 
 `message_end` can replace a finalized message while preserving its role. `tool_call` can mutate input or block execution. `tool_result` handlers compose, with each handler seeing prior changes.
